+---
+id: task-004-hourly-rental-pricing
+type: task
+title: "Hourly rental pricing"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Hourly rental pricing
+
+## Request
+
+Many visitors only want a board for an afternoon, and today we turn them away. Customers should be able
+to rent by the hour.
+
+`addEquipment` now also accepts an `hourlyPrice`, the cost of one hour of rental. A rental shorter than a
+day that starts and ends on the hour is priced at the item's hourly price for each hour. An item without
+an hourly price cannot be rented by the hour.
+
+## School rules (requirements)
+
+- R1. Money is an integer number of euro cents.
+- R3. A rental of a day or more covers whole days: start and end are at midnight UTC, and the end is the
+  start of the day after the last rented day. (task-001; unchanged for whole-day rentals)
+- H1. A rental shorter than a day, starting and ending on the hour (UTC), is priced at `hourlyPrice` for
+  each hour. Hourly rentals do not take the 10% discount of task-003.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- AC1. `addEquipment` accepts an optional `hourlyPrice`, a non-negative integer number of euro cents. A
+  non-integer or negative hourly price is rejected. (R1)
+- AC2. `quote` for a rental shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour returns
+  `hourlyPrice * hours`. (H1)
+- AC3. `book` returns the same total as `quote` for the same hourly period. (H1)
+- AC4. A rental of 1 hour and a rental spanning midnight (for example 22:00 to 02:00) are both priced by
+  the hour. (H1)
+- AC5. An item without an hourly price is refused for an hourly rental, with an error. Whole-day rentals of
+  that item are unaffected. (H1)
+- AC6. A period shorter than a day that does not start and end on the hour (for example 09:30 to 10:30) is
+  refused. (R3, H1)
+- AC7. A period of a day or more that does not start and end at midnight UTC (for example 09:00 for 24
+  hours) is refused, as before. (R3)
+- AC8. Hourly bookings take part in the overlap rules: two hourly periods that overlap for the same item
+  clash; periods that only touch do not. (task-001)
+- AC9. Errors for unknown items and for `end` not after `start` are unchanged. (task-001 AC5, AC6)
+- AC10. Availability is unchanged: `availability` still takes midnight-to-midnight periods. Hourly bookings
+  count as occupying the item for the part of the day they cover.
+
+## Test plan
+
+Test first (red, then green). Each acceptance criterion has at least one happy-path test and one
+error-path or edge-path test. Tests are deterministic: no wall-clock time, no randomness, no external
+services.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Hourly availability queries (`availability` remains day-based).
+- Discounts for hourly rentals, minimum charges, and rounding of partial hours.
+- Cancellations, refunds, and persistence across restarts.
+
+## Build record
+
+- Tests first: 9 new tests in `tests/rental.test.ts` (a `hourly rental` group: hourly price validation,
+  one hour, several hours, a rental spanning midnight, almost a day, book equals quote, no hourly price,
+  whole-day rentals unaffected, off-the-hour and non-midnight refusals, clashes and touching periods, and
+  availability). Red before the change: 9 failing, 48 passing.
+- Implementation: `src/index.ts`. `Equipment` gains an optional `hourlyPrice`, validated as a non-negative
+  integer of cents. Periods now parse on the hour; a span shorter than a day is priced at
+  `hourlyPrice * hours` (no discount), and a day or more must start and end at midnight UTC as before.
+  `availability` keeps its midnight-to-midnight query and refuses hourly queries.
+- Result: `npm test` passes, 57 of 57 (48 existing and 9 new). Type-checking with `tsc` was not run: no
+  TypeScript compiler is installed in this repository.
+- Choices made: a span of exactly 24 hours is a day, so it needs midnight start and end; hourly
+  rentals are not discounted; availability stays day-based, so an hourly booking blocks its whole day in
+  `availability`.
